* Notes about clautolisp-multidocument-analysis.org

R18 - Breakpoint table placement

    Actually the user must be able to decide whether a breakpoint is
    global (applying to the function in whatever document it's loaded
    (eg. with vl-load-all, or with separate load), or if it applies only
    to the current document.


    The default should be that the breakpoint command applies only to the
    current document, but an auxliary word ('all') could indicate that the
    command applies to all occurences of the function/break-point in all
    documents.


R19 — Concurrent debugger contexts

    Indeed, and each debugging context may route to a different user
    interface (dumb, ncurses, aldb).



* Notes about clautolisp-host-interace-spec.org

We could add mention of cadtui when nihil, cador, and <wire-host> are enumerated.
cadtui implements all cad operations using a ncurses text UI.

* Resolved (2026-11-04, documentation only)

- clautolisp-multidocument-analysis.org: R18 records the decision
  (breakpoint scope chosen by the user, current document by default, =all=
  for every document); R19 records the confirmation and that each debugging
  context may route to its own UI (dumb, ncurses, aldb).
- clautolisp-host-interface-spec.org 0.3.1: cadtui named beside nihil and
  cador where the hosts are enumerated (§2.3, §2.4); §1 and the fidelity
  matrix already described it.
- Implementing R18 / R19 belongs to the multidocument epic, not to this
  note.
